{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":493512,"name":"Sohail chahal","username":"Sohail_chahal","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/41988e/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T06:10:31.665Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/8/6/866a6c2530dbd4174f4b3626a4766602283805d1.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/jb5ZnPN9KfC96ggFQ72jF7KCMDf.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"cursorbug\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/8/6/866a6c2530dbd4174f4b3626a4766602283805d1_2_355x500.jpeg\" alt=\"cursorbug\" data-base62-sha1=\"jb5ZnPN9KfC96ggFQ72jF7KCMDf\" width=\"355\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/8/6/866a6c2530dbd4174f4b3626a4766602283805d1_2_355x500.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/8/6/866a6c2530dbd4174f4b3626a4766602283805d1.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/8/6/866a6c2530dbd4174f4b3626a4766602283805d1.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"373737\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003ecursorbug\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e446×628 36.9 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003eFor the last 3 days, Cursor is frequently blocking my Agent requests with a “Request blocked – model provider’s usage guidelines” message. I’m working on a legitimate backend project and only implementing checks/features according to my client’s requirements. The requests are normal development tasks, but they are being randomly flagged even when there is no harmful, abusive, or unauthorized intent. This is disrupting development and happens repeatedly across different requests.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-19T11:31:04.365Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":78,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":391.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171965,"topic_slug":"cursor-agent-requests-randomly-blocked-by-model-provider","display_username":"Sohail chahal","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138309,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/cursor-agent-requests-randomly-blocked-by-model-provider/171965/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":495666,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-19T11:30:14.853Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report and for the screenshot with the Request ID.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour prompt looks fine. This isn’t something in your project or setup. The block is coming from a content filter on the model side that Auto picked for these requests. Over the last few days, that filter has been mistakenly flagging some normal dev prompts like pasted logs, stack traces, hostnames, and DB status or field logic as sensitive. This is a known issue, we’re tracking it with the provider, but I can’t share an ETA yet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat should unblock you right now:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn the model picker at the bottom of the chat, switch from Auto to a specific model for these requests, like Claude or GPT. You can switch back to Auto later.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf you want to stay on Auto, trim pasted logs and error output down to one or two key lines and remove hostnames and ports before sending.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the issue happens again on a specific model already, not through Auto, send a fresh Request ID using right upper corner of chat \u0026gt; Copy Request ID in the error block and we’ll take a closer look.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-19T11:30:14.853Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":10,"readers_count":9,"score":12.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171965,"topic_slug":"cursor-agent-requests-randomly-blocked-by-model-provider","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/cursor-agent-requests-randomly-blocked-by-model-provider/171965/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_a